import ../../site/games/river/controller.dl
import site_fixture.dl

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set view's active to true
set view's frame seconds to 0.016
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
initialize the website river in (the address of state)
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river") in (the address of state)
require condition (state's river's audio's status = 1) reporting "Opening River did not load its sounds"
set buffers to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
set index to 1
loop while index <= 7:
    add (a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is index, JSON number "duration" is 2.0]) to the JSON array buffers
    increment index
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON child "buffers" is buffers]
receive website river audio reply in (the address of state)
free reply
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
set audio to the address of (state's river's audio)
require condition (((audio's voices + 0)'s id != 0) and ((audio's voices + 1)'s id != 0)) reporting "Visible River did not start music and ambience"
require condition (audio's idle request != 0) reporting "An idle River did not schedule its sheep"
set {last request} to state's requests' id
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition (state's requests' id = {last request}) reporting "An unchanged audio state kept issuing platform requests"
receive website river idle deadline in (the address of state)
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition (((audio's voices + 3)'s id != 0) and (audio's mouth > 0.0)) reporting "The idle sheep did not bellow"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-audio") in (the address of state)
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition ((audio's audible = false) and (((audio's voices + 3)'s id = 0) and (audio's idle request = 0))) reporting "Muting did not stop idle cues and timers"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-audio") in (the address of state)
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
set {program index} to the website program for source "River source"
set program to state's programs + {program index}
set program's phase to 1
notice website river start {program index} in (the address of state)
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition (audio's idle request = 0) reporting "Compiling a plan left its idle timer running"
set event to a new website river event
set event's kind to 3
set state's river's event to the address of event
set state's river's playing and state's river's active to true
set state's river's stage to 1
set state's river's speed to 2
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition (((audio's voices + 2)'s cue = 5) and ((audio's voices + 2)'s rate = 2.0)) reporting "Crossing did not start a speed-controlled rowing cue"
set state's river's active to false
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition ((audio's voices + 2)'s rate = 0.0) reporting "Pausing the game did not pause its trace sound"
set state's river's active to true
set state's river's speed to 4
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition ((audio's voices + 2)'s rate = 4.0) reporting "Resuming at another speed did not update the trace cue"
receive website river voice 2 in (the address of state)
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible true
require condition ((audio's voices + 2)'s id = 0) reporting "A finished short cue restarted inside the same instruction"
advance the website river audio in (the address of state) visible false
require condition ((audio's audible = false) and ((audio's voices + 0)'s volume = 0.0)) reporting "Hidden River music did not fade out"
fail website river audio in (the address of state)
require condition ((audio's status = 3) and ((audio's voices + 0)'s id = 0)) reporting "An audio failure retained playing resources"
# A failed play reply has already relinquished its request before cleanup.
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-audio") in (the address of state)
set buffers to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
set index to 1
loop while index <= 7:
    add (a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is (index + 10), JSON number "duration" is 2.0]) to the JSON array buffers
    increment index
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON child "buffers" is buffers]
receive website river audio reply in (the address of state)
free reply
play website river sound 2 in slot 2 at offset 0.0 in (the address of state)
set consumed to state's requests
set state's requests to consumed's next
deallocate consumed
fail website river audio after purpose 13 indexed 2 in (the address of state)
require condition ((audio's voices + 2)'s request = 0) reporting "Failure cleanup tried to cancel its consumed play request"
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
free state's river's coding
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "River audio owns decoding, idle deadlines, muting, visibility, cue boundaries, pause, speed and failure cleanup in DynLex."
